  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 205 PM EDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nAs we approach the end of the work week, we continue to hold on to \nunseasonably warm temperatures across much of the CWA. Highs in the \nlow to mid 90s with apparent temperatures in the triple digits will \ncontinue into the weekend.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n20% for much of the area through the week. The ridge is finally \nexpected to break down Sunday into Monday as a front approaches. \nIsolated thunderstorms will be possible on Sunday afternoon, \nbecoming more widespread on Monday but total rainfall is expected to \nbe less than an inch for much of the CWA through the forecast \nperiod. \n\nThe front will bring afternoon thunderstorms back into the forecast \nto start off next week. This will help to moderate temps down to the \nupper 80s and low 90s, but still warm for this time of year.",
